Lobium — native clientRects farbling (seeds.clientRects).

Perturbs Element::getClientRects / GetBoundingClientRect by a stable sub-pixel delta so float
geometry fingerprints differ per profile without changing layout. Guarded on seeds.clientRects != 0.

The kernel keys the delta on the rect's own VALUES, not on a call index. That matters: honest Chrome
returns exactly equal doubles whenever geometry coincides — a child that fills its parent, one
element's bottom against the next one's top, two identically laid-out elements. Index keying gave
those independent nudges and broke every such equality, which is a handful of lines of JS to detect.
Value keying gives equal inputs equal outputs, so the relations survive; it also makes the two call
sites below agree by construction rather than by both happening to pass index 0.

